<section id="S5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.6. </span>Parameter Study (RQ4)</h3>

<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23235v1/aitw_curr_his_hp_ablation2.svg" id="S5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/175;" width="476" height="175"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="S5.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameter sensitivity analysis on AITW.<span id="S5.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We evaluate the Step SR under varying compression intensities: the impact of the temporal decay factor <math id="S5.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in TAR, and the impact of the background saliency factor <math id="S5.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in SSP.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using Qwen2-VL-2B on AITW, we analyze the sensitivity of the temporal decay factor <math id="S5.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the background saliency factor <math id="S5.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, and the pruning layer depth <math id="S5.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter Sensitivity (<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho</annotation></semantics></math>).</span> The results are visualized in Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.6. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ Spatio-Temporal Token Pruning for Efficient High-Resolution GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, which presents performance curves across three distinct compression rates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(1) Temporal Decay Factor <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> With current frame retention fixed at 100%, we vary <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the coefficient governing decay steepness (<math id="S5.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> signifies uniformity). As shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.6. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ Spatio-Temporal Token Pruning for Efficient High-Resolution GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (Left), performance peaks at <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and monotonically degrades as <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\to 1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\to 1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. This confirms that prioritizing immediate history is superior to a uniform distribution, aligning with the agent’s reliance on high-fidelity recent context.
<span id="S5.SS6.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(2) Background Saliency Factor <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Conversely, with history frames fully retained to isolate spatial effects, we analyze <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, which modulates the trade-off between local saliency and global structure. Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.6. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ Spatio-Temporal Token Pruning for Efficient High-Resolution GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (Right) reveals a distinct peak at <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>. Deviations cause degradation: higher <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> sacrifices layout integrity, while lower <math id="S5.SS6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> captures insufficient semantic context, verifying that a balanced allocation is critical.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pruning Layer Depth (<math id="S5.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>).</span> With retention ratios fixed at <math id="S5.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>, we systematically investigate the efficiency-performance trade-off by varying the pruning layer insertion depth <math id="S5.SS6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.6. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ Spatio-Temporal Token Pruning for Efficient High-Resolution GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, results reveal a distinct non-monotonic trend.
Pruning at the earliest stage (<math id="S5.SS6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math>) precipitates a performance collapse (12.4% Step SR) accompanied by an anomalous surge in FLOPs (3.79T). We attribute this to the immature attention patterns in the first layer, which fail to reliably distinguish interactive semantic regions. This leads to severe grounding hallucinations and output formatting errors, triggering verbose, incorrect generation that paradoxically inflates the total computational cost.
In contrast, Layer 2 emerges as the optimal operating point, achieving peak performance (65.3%) while minimizing computational overhead (3.39T). Beyond this point (<math id="S5.SS6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>), performance gradually degrades, and FLOPs linearly increase as additional shallow layers expend resources on the full token sequence before pruning occurs. Qualitative visualizations of attention maps and extended analysis are provided in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Analysis of Pruning Depth ‣ Spatio-Temporal Token Pruning for Efficient High-Resolution GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>. </span><span id="S5.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Parameter study on the pruning layer depth (<math id="S5.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>) for SSP.<span id="S5.T5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We analyze the trade-off between navigation performance (Step SR) and computational cost (FLOPs) by varying the layer index where pruning is executed.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T5.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:50.6pt;vertical-align:-21.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(45.6pt,-6.7pt) scale(1.35900983431321,1.35900983431321) ;">
<table id="S5.T5.6.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T5.6.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><math id="S5.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.6.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">Step SR</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">12.4</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">65.3</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">64.4</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">61.1</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">60.6</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.6.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">FLOPs (T)</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">3.79</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3.39</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">3.45</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">3.48</td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">3.53</td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
